.TH PKILL 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkill \- signal processes whose command name matches a pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkill
.RB [ \-SIGNAL ]
.I pattern
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send a signal (default
.BR SIGTERM )
to every process whose command name matches
.IR pattern ,
using the exact same matching
.BR pgrep (1)
does. Accepts the same signal forms as
.BR kill (1):
.BR \-9 / \-KILL ,
.BR \-15 / \-TERM ,
.BR \-1 / \-HUP ,
.BR \-2 / \-INT ,
or a bare
.BI \- n
for signal number
.IR n .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every matching process was signaled successfully, 1 if none
matched or any signal failed, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pgrep (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
